<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow,noarchive">
    <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
    <title>Mark organization traffic</title>
    {% if standalone|default(false) %}
        {# Downloaded HTML bundles the source stylesheet to stay portable. #}
        <style>{% include '@styles/internal-traffic.css' %}</style>
    {% else %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/internal-traffic.css') }}" referrerpolicy="no-referrer">
    {% endif %}
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <h1>Mark organization traffic</h1>
    <p>Use this page to identify your browser as a team member’s browser, so your own visits can be filtered out of analytics reports. Nothing is written until you choose.</p>
    {% if marking %}
        {% include 'internal_traffic/websites.html.twig' %}
        <h2>This analytics site</h2>
        <p>These buttons mark only this site{% if browser_config.storage == 'cookie' and browser_config.cookieDomain %} and the other websites under {{ browser_config.cookieDomain }}, which share its cookie{% endif %}. Use the links above for your tracked websites.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% include 'internal_traffic/marker.html.twig' %}
    <p>Every event from a tracked website reports <code>"org_internal_traffic": true</code> when the browser carries the marker on that website, and <code>false</code> otherwise. It identifies traffic from your organization, independently of navigation within a website.</p>
    <p>{% if browser_config.storage == 'cookie' %}The marker is a cookie that lasts up to one year. Browsers may clear it earlier.{% else %}The marker is kept in local storage, which belongs to one exact origin (scheme, hostname and port), until it is removed or cleared.{% endif %}</p>
    {% if download_url %}
        <p>For a website whose home page does not load the tracker, <a href="{{ download_url }}" download="internal-traffic.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">download an HTML marker page</a>, host it on that website and open it there. The download contains the marker settings and no share token.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <p>This marker affects reporting only. It does not grant access to any account. Mark each browser and device you want to exclude.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
